<title>COLOMBIA: RESEARCH ALERT-Carulla upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Carulla upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santander Investment said it was upgrading Colombian retailer Carulla, one of the country's biggest supermarket chains, to market perform from underperform on a relative valuation basis.</p>
<p>-- Santander said it had set a 12-month target price of $4.50 for Carulla's shares, a level that implies 13 percent upside from current levels.</p>
<p>-- It said Carulla should see a 35 percent increase in operating profits this year, in dollar terms, and net profit growth of 13.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- &quot;The company is working at improving efficiency and cutting costs,&quot; Santander added, saying operating expenses as a percentage of sales fell to 22.9 percent in the first quarter from 23.7 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
